    {
      "text": "Combine ketchup, bourbon, and brown sugar in a saucepan over medium heat. Cook and stir until sugar dissolves, 2 to 3 minutes. Add hot dogs. Cover and simmer for 1 hour.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/2XF7deUR7vG8I1b15wS3T9G4Elg=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/278005-bourbon-hot-dogs-VAT-007-step-02-b49bec85f5264637a6563cd09e9f26f8.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/278005/step_02.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Let cool completely before refrigerating for 24 to 48 hours.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/yx6uUn81DQigPQzdcA8oZ7_MNtc=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/278005-bourbon-hot-dogs-VAT-008-step-03-b81c60364ada4935aad4e6516dc48b6f.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/278005/step_03.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Reheat hot dogs by simmering in a pan over medium heat, about 5 minutes. Serve warm with toothpicks.",
